title: Sharing, several scripts, saving, and two things at once
card: Chapter 9 | Names the whole program shares | The world remembers
say:
  A name set inside a command belongs to that command, and disappears when it ends.
  Names that every command shares go in a block called: the world remembers.
uncard
files: scores.fathom
open: scores.fathom
zoom: lines 1-10
spot: line 1
say: This script was written earlier. The first line is a whisper: a note for people. The computer ignores it.
spot: lines 3-5
say:
  The world remembers high scores, a table of numbers. Every command in the program can read it and change it.
  Shared names start empty: zero, no, empty text, or an empty list or table.
spot: lines 7-10
say:
  Record keeps a player's points, if they're new, or better than before.
spot: off
zoom: out

card: Chapter 9 | Several scripts | One program, made of many files
say: A bigger program is easier to keep in several scripts. Let's make a game that uses this one.
uncard
new: game.fathom
type:
  use: scores.fathom

  the world remembers:
    games played (a number)
  and the universe said i love you

  to play a round, given player (text) and points (a number):
    set games played to games played plus 1
    record with (player, points)
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    play a round with ("Sam", 31)
    play a round with ("Jo", 7)
    play a round with ("Sam", 12)
    scrawl games played, " games. Best scores: ", high scores as saved text
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 1-5
spot: line 1
say:
  Use scores dot fathom brings in that script's commands, kinds, and shared names. It's looked for next to this one.
  Its genesis is left out, so each script can still be run and tried by itself.
spot: lines 3-5
say: This script remembers its own shared name too: how many games were played.
spot: off
zoom: lines 7-10
say: Play a round counts the game, and uses record, from the other script.
zoom: lines 12-17
spot: line 16
say:
  As saved text writes any value as JSON: the text format websites and other programs use. Load from the text reads it back.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
say: Three games, and the best scores: Jo seven, Sam thirty one. Sam's twelve wasn't better, so it wasn't kept.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 9 | Saving and loading | Remembering between runs
say: When the program ends, its names are gone. To remember high scores for next time, save them in a file.
uncard
line: 16
type:

    save high scores to file "scores.json"
line: 12
type:

    if file "scores.json" exists: load high scores from file "scores.json"
zoom: lines 12-18
spot: line 13
say:
  If the file exists, load high scores from it. Load needs a name that already holds the right kind of value, here, a table of numbers.
spot: line 18
say: And at the end, save writes them to the file. Lists, tables, places and your own kinds of things can all be saved, even inside each other.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
say: The first run saves the scores. Now let's change the game, and run it again.
line: 14
keys: end
keys: backspace backspace backspace
type: 50)
run
zoom: output
say: Sam scored fifty, and that beat the thirty one that was loaded from the file.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 9 | Two things at once | Meanwhile
say: Last in this chapter: doing two things at the same time.
uncard
new: both.fathom
type:
  to count, given who (text) and gap (a number):
    for each n from 1 to 3:
      wait gap
      scrawl who, " ", n
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    meanwhile count with ("fast", 0.3)
    meanwhile count with ("slow", 0.5)
    wait for the others
    scrawl "Both done."
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 1-5
say: Count waits a moment between numbers. Wait comes from the time library, and gap says how many seconds.
zoom: lines 7-12
spot: lines 8-9
say:
  Meanwhile starts a command going on its own, and the next line carries on straight away. So both counters run at once.
spot: line 10
say: Wait for the others waits until everything started with meanwhile has finished.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
say: Fast and slow take turns, each at its own speed, and then: both done.
wait
zoom: out
